#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092093 :question/id #uuid "57034318-5a6e-53f6-a8d3-ae8c61692947" :question/math-academy-id "e-641" :question/problem "![](images/0b/0bb9e5e7315d4bcd5fc21700fdd2597f6d9b585a109145de53c6f94e9530eabf.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=2(1-\\cos\\theta)$ for $0 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\pi$ (shown in blue in the picture above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL =  \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2 }\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta.\n$$\n\nSince $r=2(1-\\cos\\theta),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta} = 2\\sin\\theta.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{8-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now use the half-angle formula $1-\\cos\\theta =2\\sin^2\\left(\\dfrac{\\theta}{2}\\right)$ to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={-4\\cdot 2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right))|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-8(0-1) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092125 :question/id #uuid "8b8e3c66-fc60-57ac-baf7-0661e213d01e" :question/math-academy-id "e-7400" :question/problem "![](images/e5/e5647c0f19727d1e626e637464cc57444e0bc0f2f8e99a4afd15d3c3631dc3f0.png)\n\nFind an integral expression for the arc length of the polar curve $r=3-\\sin(7\\theta)$ for $0 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\pi,$ shown in blue in the diagram above." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL =  \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2 }\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta.\n$$\n\nSince $r=3-\\sin(7\\theta),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta} =-7\\cos(7\\theta)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(3-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta ))^{2}+(-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )+49{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )+{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )+48{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta )+1+48{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{10-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta )+48{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092571 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9841d5a0-2d6c-5f87-a27a-f94eefabc095" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π/2}e^{θ}\\sqrt{2θ^{2} + 4θ + 1}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089598} {:answer/id #uuid "29dd10e3-97bd-56a6-b470-31427419f7fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π/2}e^{θ}\\sqrt{4θ^{2} + 2θ + 1}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089599} {:answer/id #uuid "33a3e6d0-52bd-58d1-a159-6de1f2c26ef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π/2}e^{θ}\\sqrt{θ^{2} + θ + 1}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089600} {:answer/id #uuid "5fbdd8df-eace-5463-a068-bbed35d03037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π/2}e^{θ}\\sqrt{2θ^{2} + 2θ + 1}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089601} {:answer/id #uuid "64f79122-83f5-593c-b841-41de68986368" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π/2}e^{θ}\\sqrt{2θ^{2} + 2θ + 2}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089602}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0639070a-f499-59b7-b57a-59e78c70795f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089597} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbc2c061-b810-50f4-998c-b4c24f1e568e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{\\theta }\\sqrt{2{\\theta }^{2}+4\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401029} {:answer/id #uuid "2da42875-db42-5de8-9dff-ef55f911995f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{\\theta }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401030} {:answer/id #uuid "1d0f9249-e37d-56d1-8c90-4ef1bb8df2ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{\\theta }\\sqrt{4{\\theta }^{2}+2\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401031} {:answer/id #uuid "21b19373-36de-5c05-9a8d-58dcde77b9ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{\\theta }\\sqrt{2{\\theta }^{2}+2\\theta +2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401032} {:answer/id #uuid "293c2bba-fb9f-5a3b-a596-e4fc57546fc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{\\theta }\\sqrt{2{\\theta }^{2}+2\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "293c2bba-fb9f-5a3b-a596-e4fc57546fc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{\\theta }\\sqrt{2{\\theta }^{2}+2\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401033} :answer-field/id #uuid "61740183-1d83-54ca-8ff3-51d0ccdbf570" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dd646452-89ff-5f38-8817-208b877e41c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-15144" :question/problem "![](images/4b/4b03822d65ec9f5bea3a1e47d25e4831470754fa09cef510e7c452cc292e9e40.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=\\theta {e}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\theta {e}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }={e}^{\\theta }+\\theta {e}^{\\theta }=(1+\\theta ){e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{(\\theta {e}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{((1+\\theta ){e}^{\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}{e}^{2\\theta }+(1+2\\theta +{\\theta }^{2}){e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(2{\\theta }^{2}+2\\theta +1){e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{\\theta }\\sqrt{2{\\theta }^{2}+2\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092764 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48fb4307-6ed3-5c9c-b575-3ba634b07a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )-4{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330604} {:answer/id #uuid "4d66b536-d432-592f-a552-3d83dea6fff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330653} {:answer/id #uuid "aed125a5-00ff-5286-9d0e-22a4dfe0b47e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331494} {:answer/id #uuid "bc622ef6-2ea5-5738-a6db-23a2ff317b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )+4{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331610} {:answer/id #uuid "c74a4616-57fa-5359-a03f-682fd7db8330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )+2{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aed125a5-00ff-5286-9d0e-22a4dfe0b47e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331494} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a1ff240-3ade-5343-b0cf-fe6ee4dd31c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332268}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c1df0a62-d91d-5d2f-932b-891ad126ab27" :question/math-academy-id "q-51198" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092922 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "190a5314-e72d-527b-aa9e-4c0079dd688c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357971} {:answer/id #uuid "1bee1bb4-be7d-5d20-8d21-32d53d01088d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357991} {:answer/id #uuid "a7a0db5f-5c7a-5f5e-a290-e7a1248188e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359199} {:answer/id #uuid "be699b03-471d-5316-a2b6-92062d60c4b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359416} {:answer/id #uuid "efdd4d3d-453e-5e4d-8a75-09e728ac5829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "190a5314-e72d-527b-aa9e-4c0079dd688c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357971} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a502992-4bc8-5b1f-9a6e-579818ef462a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dfaa6223-b113-5398-adeb-e8d8b6d36965" :question/math-academy-id "q-9532" :question/problem "![](images/08/085be1e624ae99afee256d2a9591f17d2f33f688364b6e59fdcd7c415206bda7.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{5\\pi }{6}\n$$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}1\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\theta {|}_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092923 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a7c6d33-ec9d-5f09-8a41-23c7079e0681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091742} {:answer/id #uuid "635d1f78-1ff1-548c-b1d2-727e82d8d662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531082} {:answer/id #uuid "ad493751-d3c8-5246-8a30-3a2a4aefa677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531239} {:answer/id #uuid "b6a466dc-34ab-5292-b042-6078d2d70c1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-{e}^{-\\pi /2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531253} {:answer/id #uuid "d7923dd0-6a1a-51d5-bb60-8f501bdb44b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\pi /2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad493751-d3c8-5246-8a30-3a2a4aefa677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531239} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4db8ae4-ea41-5588-80ee-f64b1cf5f458" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d05250f7-7ca4-5099-862d-2ef2f12670bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-9536" :question/problem "![](images/fa/fa58c9d1c0680dd94bb25c04e0a268df836e14bfb217f0a20d3bd75224cec4e8.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r={e}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={e}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }={e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{({e}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{({e}^{\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2\\theta }+{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\theta }{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235501 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9d00ec8-e865-5151-9a4c-bad4652bfb11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9d00ec8-e865-5151-9a4c-bad4652bfb11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234805} :answer-field/id #uuid "079110b6-6c4b-5d0b-9a1e-a17faca83de8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2f543150-38e4-557e-9ab8-57056b911cc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-167938" :question/problem "Construct and simplify an integral representing the arc length of this circle using polar coordinates.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n${\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n{{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n$\\,\\,\\text{d}\\theta $" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{36({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}6\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238061 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11ab5490-6958-5907-9744-daca5ba83c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )-6{sin}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235917} {:answer/id #uuid "23a1d755-1a8c-5412-a736-df2f34a61feb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )+36{sin}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236046} {:answer/id #uuid "2e0f10c6-f01a-58b2-9e7c-e6f93eb8b719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )+6{cos}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236109} {:answer/id #uuid "8c5e3191-58c4-58b2-85d9-7d6953772bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236705} {:answer/id #uuid "96af5361-9440-53c2-b581-6ff64a3f4000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )-{cos}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23a1d755-1a8c-5412-a736-df2f34a61feb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )+36{sin}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236046} :answer-field/id #uuid "051b7d4c-b18a-50b8-837c-5476d5b85f2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237448}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "616e09b3-d157-50df-b328-51943da5bea6" :question/math-academy-id "q-103832" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta )$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{12}?$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta ),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta ))^{2}+(-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )+36{sin}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238062 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e00f277-5143-5957-904d-a9dd31eb0a89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235892} {:answer/id #uuid "24bfddc8-84e0-588a-8616-05b13b833b55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236054} {:answer/id #uuid "2ffac8cf-a6de-5f8b-b74d-5b6a9c38c64d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236123} {:answer/id #uuid "3673d5cc-88d2-50a8-a857-56a93c0d35f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236165} {:answer/id #uuid "5727ed7b-95e5-5433-8814-34b439a62973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5727ed7b-95e5-5433-8814-34b439a62973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236369} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe185be0-4aea-5d12-8405-2c55fa532bf9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237772}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "aaa400a5-0216-5218-b483-3ceee85bd49a" :question/math-academy-id "q-103834" :question/problem "![](images/1b/1bd01b4fe70a497cc66811a2d5b070908221b9932655ee396d9a8039471702c2.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi $ (shown in blue in the diagram above)?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238064 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47084e96-4575-5ea2-bc29-d0119689a067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236272} {:answer/id #uuid "5c665951-8f9f-5315-b3f3-bac47dafdacc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236396} {:answer/id #uuid "8127b6a0-4402-576d-a67a-897bdcc56f58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236622} {:answer/id #uuid "d6287872-577f-5bdf-aa77-b5a797c91de2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237171} {:answer/id #uuid "ef3ea81c-a5ed-52a6-801d-d9a3a71605f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47084e96-4575-5ea2-bc29-d0119689a067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236272} :answer-field/id #uuid "eca36830-c9ce-5e40-8c39-1b9f25663b85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237744}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "57b3d195-da37-5216-80d4-504f546a07a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-103837" :question/problem "![](images/33/3387790df770ac8645058c6f460b1f1285629d18d765668e362a8070ae4035ed.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi $ (shown in blue in the diagram above).\n\n*Hint: You may wish to use the following identity: $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}.\n$$*" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{8+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall the identity for $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right):$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using $x=\\theta $ in the previous identity, the integral can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={4\\cdot 2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right))|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =8(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238068 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10eb4957-edbb-5cdb-ac64-9bc72c43dea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235908} {:answer/id #uuid "acce3f64-38d4-545c-a90a-98ae08560f34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236916} {:answer/id #uuid "d622bbba-38b9-58f1-aec8-b7200b12def3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237170} {:answer/id #uuid "e015dcfd-6510-5e73-8639-a91aea104895" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237223} {:answer/id #uuid "fefc8cb9-5106-5ba6-8509-ba84de8e6560" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acce3f64-38d4-545c-a90a-98ae08560f34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236916} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bfbd4d3-1699-53a9-8de9-e66feb8a6c94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237623}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "96931358-f8ea-56cc-a85a-c2b66216308c" :question/math-academy-id "q-103842" :question/problem "![](images/03/038d135bd0d8d163808fe21be0159a1a08db37c3e33599c97033ca0d53abab36.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{7\\pi }{4}\n$$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{7\\pi /4}\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{7\\pi /4}\\sqrt{4({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{7\\pi /4}1\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\theta {|}_{3\\pi /2}^{7\\pi /4} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275260 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f627df1-adde-57f5-90e4-09efa69ff493" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+9{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272664} {:answer/id #uuid "9adcea7e-7161-588b-9a67-61c17173cfeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+3{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273726} {:answer/id #uuid "cc6f3505-29fa-5085-abdb-d93a28a2158d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+9{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274166} {:answer/id #uuid "dfa293b5-f3ac-5c8b-a37b-f89a115d333f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+3{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274364} {:answer/id #uuid "e71092c7-0d47-53dd-a9ce-c8db47ee94d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+9{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc6f3505-29fa-5085-abdb-d93a28a2158d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+9{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274166} :answer-field/id #uuid "be32e887-d36f-5576-8d64-d4f02bbc18f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274970}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8ac3b5b3-7e20-5bd6-a6af-097e3f624a37" :question/math-academy-id "q-15122" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )$ for $$\n\\displaystyle -\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{6}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta ),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta ))^{2}+(-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+36{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\sqrt{4({cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+9{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta ))}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+9{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275261 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c54104b-b3dc-5569-a45f-4825e0d27a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{10-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )+8{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272635} {:answer/id #uuid "6bb5aa76-e451-50b2-91fb-baabb9a3700f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{10-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )+8{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273315} {:answer/id #uuid "ae56957b-c439-5d47-a819-1031c5bf0206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{10-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )+8{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273892} {:answer/id #uuid "c676dbe5-5207-5293-af38-9e035d17772c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )+8{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274109} {:answer/id #uuid "f54e6d65-362a-5898-9764-0fd2e605a7d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )+9{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274550}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae56957b-c439-5d47-a819-1031c5bf0206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{10-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )+8{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273892} :answer-field/id #uuid "c075fa06-e768-565d-b8b4-20d1444a6cc1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e06591c4-f9ec-5725-a82d-146c8f26267d" :question/math-academy-id "q-15129" :question/problem "![](images/59/59214bcbfd4b1d718faa0c2355e932ab3cedae5b785b17497cef554ee3ec099b.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=3-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=3-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta ),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(3-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta ))^{2}+(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )+{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+9{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )+1+8{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{10-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )+8{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275263 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41612c4c-f870-5ed5-87f8-b382715e8648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+2{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272945} {:answer/id #uuid "751d78c4-b19a-5d89-b496-847e248ea026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+4{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273388} {:answer/id #uuid "afd5220f-e133-5338-b18e-873ee1f218a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+4{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273908} {:answer/id #uuid "b03474d7-bd8f-5753-8615-74c0bc59287d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+3{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273913} {:answer/id #uuid "db564748-e979-5e7d-9d93-c9c418e8c841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+3{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b03474d7-bd8f-5753-8615-74c0bc59287d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+3{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273913} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba365ec3-d4cf-55b8-8901-8ccc6da95432" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274959}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "915da383-5cd0-54bd-ae8a-9f0bc95c9cf2" :question/math-academy-id "q-15131" :question/problem "![](images/00/00e5e0f5c47a056beaca2d7bc1b1d10a6a11f96398df7400e69c023f5780b8a6.png)\n\nWhich of the following integrals gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $$\n\\displaystyle -\\,\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}\n$$ (shown in blue in the  diagram above)?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )+4{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+1+3{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+3{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287977 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "350096c6-a564-5b13-9323-1f11b8aa5aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{\\pi /4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285275} {:answer/id #uuid "356014bd-2e78-54b8-b0b0-a26c4f89ea3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285277} {:answer/id #uuid "afb947fe-8e6d-5b21-8c84-9d36b0e511e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-{e}^{-\\pi /4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286390} {:answer/id #uuid "c2105640-4979-51fa-87a3-fc2d8a9feddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286564} {:answer/id #uuid "f5026c60-d19c-5056-93eb-03f4608bdbda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\pi /4}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2105640-4979-51fa-87a3-fc2d8a9feddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286564} :answer-field/id #uuid "059711ce-e66a-51ec-8839-dd341320f202" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287157}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "feb9e004-f407-5daf-8181-931953281eea" :question/math-academy-id "q-20070" :question/problem "![](images/fa/fa1c1c3ae2769f45854de4f0b00fc394fccb40b40704cfd09e6eb11eee3c07af.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=3{e}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=3{e}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=3{e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{(3{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{(3{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{e}^{2\\theta }+9{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{18{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{e}^{\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\theta }{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319211 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc63ae4e-cfaa-53ce-820b-6b955f4e241e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{\\pi /8}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc63ae4e-cfaa-53ce-820b-6b955f4e241e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{\\pi /8}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318407} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c3bf0c6-3804-5ad7-986b-8aafdaaff36d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dc5a81b5-b9fd-57fc-867d-023dfe7eb508" :question/math-academy-id "q-347926" :question/problem "![](images/2d/2da83e2ec620d3920c4378a77785a9ef2802dd1d06badcf4852be2263f68264e.png)\n\nFind the arc length $L$ of the polar curve $r=6{e}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{8}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=6\\sqrt{2}($\n{{field-1}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=6{e}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=6{e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{{(6{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{(6{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{36{e}^{2\\theta }+36{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{72{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}{e}^{\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\theta }{|}_{0}^{\\pi /8} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /8}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /8}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321141 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd1ec179-c3eb-579d-b407-4fb26d5fa6e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}({e}^{\\pi }-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320154} {:answer/id #uuid "048e136b-84ec-5868-b091-1a12da7bcf24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}(e^{\\pi}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "048e136b-84ec-5868-b091-1a12da7bcf24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}(e^{\\pi}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498739} :answer-field/id #uuid "2092fbc0-9454-5cb0-afd6-99345b4a8c65" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e21eed1a-d586-5617-ae1f-53bbb8801576" :question/math-academy-id "q-353598" :question/problem "![](images/16/16b676776dc22aece5a1fa777007a03b9e7903706cbdf5cc4ae14d8508370419.png)\n\nFind the arc length $L$ of the polar curve $r={e}^{2\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={e}^{2\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=2{e}^{2\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{({e}^{2\\theta })}^{2}+{(2{e}^{2\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{e}^{4\\theta }+4{e}^{4\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{5{e}^{4\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}{[\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2\\theta }]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{[{e}^{2\\theta }]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}({e}^{2(\\pi /2)}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}({e}^{\\pi }-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321143 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ec07961-28ad-57ab-9dc2-935afbeeb1e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319580}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ec07961-28ad-57ab-9dc2-935afbeeb1e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319580} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcb6204f-3eb4-5f37-91f5-6c3112218559" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4c077a15-44c0-5080-9f91-c561226617cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-353605" :question/problem "Find the arc length $L$ of the polar curve $r={3}^{\\theta /4}$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le 4.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}$\\sqrt{{ln}^{2}⁡3+16}$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={3}^{\\theta /4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }={3}^{\\theta /4}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{{({3}^{\\theta /4})}^{2}+{({3}^{\\theta /4}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{{3}^{\\theta /2}+{3}^{\\theta /2}\\cdot \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡3}{16}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{(1+\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡3}{16}){3}^{\\theta /2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡3}{16}}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{3}^{\\theta /4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡3}{16}}\\cdot \\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot {3}^{\\theta /4}\\,{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡3}{16}}\\cdot \\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot ({3}^{1}-{3}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡3}{16}}\\cdot \\frac{8}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\sqrt{{ln}^{2}⁡3+16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332861 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41568bc8-66e5-5b92-91c4-58bf4fc1454e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5({e}^{\\pi /6}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330528} {:answer/id #uuid "54db32e5-e7f2-5e11-aad2-ade2bfba19a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /6}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330715} {:answer/id #uuid "a2d1d05c-6a03-5691-a924-a5b82477104f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /6}-e)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331410} {:answer/id #uuid "bd415b93-19f9-5d77-9f40-160be3444725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{e}^{\\pi /6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331620} {:answer/id #uuid "ef74e128-de92-54ef-9418-a05286dd0154" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\pi /6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54db32e5-e7f2-5e11-aad2-ade2bfba19a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /6}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330715} :answer-field/id #uuid "575b490b-6032-578f-8fda-8c94315455f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0690f2a6-3e10-52f0-a935-4f8552e1024c" :question/math-academy-id "q-51201" :question/problem "![](images/80/8076c5991e4c66bb505fa1800ce3d78fab0fc115560ef59efb72e6776976c977.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=5{e}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{6}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=5{e}^{\\theta },$ wehave\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=5{e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{(5{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{(5{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\sqrt{25{e}^{2\\theta }+25{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\sqrt{50{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}{e}^{\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\theta }{|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /6}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /6}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367610 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ce484f3-4e5e-550d-818e-f1c78bea979f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{26+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )+24{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367612} {:answer/id #uuid "cedb54b5-de63-5342-98e6-7ed2532c1269" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{25+1