is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=5+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta ),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(5+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta ))^{2}+(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{25+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )+25{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{25+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )+1+24{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{26+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )+24{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368473 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3226b3d-5b7b-5998-9e41-3291da5e0ec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3226b3d-5b7b-5998-9e41-3291da5e0ec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368475} :answer-field/id #uuid "43d5cd64-97a3-504d-8d46-2dc8153e9473" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "035f0c13-8d58-5770-be30-4f6df395cfa7" :question/math-academy-id "q-353383" :question/problem "![](images/d8/d8a2a7761f3bacee21d61c5212864cf5f4fe2e44198789b80f1655af73d78d53.png)\n\nFind the arc length $L$ of the polar curve $r=9\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=9\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{(9\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{81{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +81{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{81}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}1\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =9\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =9(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368927 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "886a46d3-862e-5cf9-bdf7-2db062a9391d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10-5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368929} {:answer/id #uuid "2080f337-f34d-5214-ae2e-1f687592ab3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20-10\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368930} {:answer/id #uuid "2317f100-b67e-576e-826b-aaef4bd21eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10+10\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368931} {:answer/id #uuid "cea28c65-6773-523e-94df-fdfadc3d2da5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20-20\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368932} {:answer/id #uuid "842fa18b-8a77-502a-8444-caa61decd99f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2080f337-f34d-5214-ae2e-1f687592ab3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20-10\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368930} :answer-field/id #uuid "82a45f10-ea66-583d-9440-7fd42435002d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "821b961c-4260-5cdb-aa68-730b1a7ce8e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-9539" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the polar curve $r=5-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to use the following identity: $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}.\n$$*" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=5-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{(5-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{25-50\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +25{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +25{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{25-50\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +25}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{50-50\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{50}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall the identity for $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right):$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using $x=\\theta $ in the previous identity, the integral can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{50}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{50}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={-10\\cdot 2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right))|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-20(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-20(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-1) \\\\  & =20-10\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399405 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6874921-2d2f-5f05-b3f8-8b581a1d8844" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399407} {:answer/id #uuid "ed64815a-d2d8-553b-a6f7-b8434bf21b56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )-{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399408} {:answer/id #uuid "98fb496d-54bd-55f2-a700-7d72677cb636" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}