}=-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta ))^{2}+(-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+144{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{16({cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+9{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta ))}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+9{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401014 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c77b2f36-6be8-50c0-ae22-868fa6cf86a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )+16{cos}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401016} {:answer/id #uuid "09d3bae4-8fa4-5410-960c-88cdf9ccbafc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )+4{cos}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401017} {:answer/id #uuid "e29d1f8d-e673-5fab-ab5a-b94d3c279c90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )+4{cos}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401018} {:answer/id #uuid "d634400e-7fcc-5b2f-8882-b33255d21d09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )+4{cos}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401019} {:answer/id #uuid "33483e89-3247-5b5b-b6c3-9a62773834b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )+16{cos}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c77b2f36-6be8-50c0-ae22-868fa6cf86a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )+16{cos}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401016} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d94100e-63ab-58cf-b2c0-0f485eafe140" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4a434871-4fea-52cd-80a4-1fd81c159fb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-15133" :question/problem "![](images/3a/3a760f55b6437a39010e4d1a00bdb5fb5390d848dd74347e7736e2ac49cd562b.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta ),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=12\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta ))^{2}+(12\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )+144{cos}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9({sin}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )+16{cos}^{2}⁡(4\\theta ))}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )+16{cos}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d63901ad-848e-5f8f-b7f4-a6f0cabcd6ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401023} {:answer/id #uuid "802cfcd0-a88b-5f37-b901-56f2fa1fec34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2{e}^{\\theta }+{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401024} {:answer/id #uuid "3d75caa2-eae0-5f0c-a250-6aa6ab5b7726" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+{e}^{\\theta }+{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401025} {:answer/id #uuid "892fe229-a636-5af2-bb7c-28f7e30053e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{e}^{\\theta }+2{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401026} {:answer/id #uuid "4d7af40e-74ed-51e2-be9d-1cf5c95c728a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2{e}^{\\theta }+2{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d7af40e-74ed-51e2-be9d-1cf5c95c728a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2{e}^{\\theta }+2{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401027} :answer-field/id #uuid "7aecd8d8-445d-5023-ad24-6e7f3a0a5ec4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401022}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c659d13d-a024-51d5-b83b-b004bef94416" :question/math-academy-id "q-15136" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=1+{e}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1+{e}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }={e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{(1+{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{({e}^{\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2{e}^{\\theta }+{e}^{2\\theta }+{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2{e}^{\\theta }+2{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446930 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10cd98c4-ea24-55c4-a79c-cf3c9ddf5714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446904} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa86582-4f58-56be-8b2e-64523909f390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )+3{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446910} {:answer/id #uuid "7b917d8d-ed20-53e9-8f2f-10a316604da1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446912} {:answer/id #uuid "bc99ca06-7d50-5d19-b832-2a97e3ac7a8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )-3{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446917} {:answer/id #uuid "d281e271-ac5c-5125-9398-f8102c7c4a4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7aa86582-4f58-56be-8b2e-64523909f390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )+3{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446910} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3650c47-b992-5daf-9894-5a44218a3232" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2855547f-5d51-5448-b3d2-5e4f3624a47a" :question/math-academy-id "q-51199" :question/problem "![](images/50/5052773d05690f49969487f5ec75a1cdd15c278c1c7552dd5d811ea2e023256c.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $$\n\\displaystyle -\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}\n$$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )+{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )+1+3{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )+3{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446931 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b4071d8-b7bd-5947-891a-3136a4368de9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b4071d8-b7bd-5947-891a-3136a4368de9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446911} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e0e99ea-5dd8-556e-b3e4-bb6d0549ec0e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "496b1e54-6c94-5491-8b44-b97586fa418a" :question/math-academy-id "q-353382" :question/problem "![](images/07/07dd1e37f29e06051c7fe84210d41857c7c871ce577c71a86781be4ce7a0ef23.png)\n\nFind the arc length $L$ of the polar curve $r=7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{(7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{49{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +49{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{49}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}7\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =7\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =7(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446932 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05141a1b-cb9e-5283-9e45-82ca469a01e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}({4}^{\\pi /2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446902} {:answer/id #uuid "13998c82-80d9-5cc7-a5a5-a3c689f79c8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}({4}^{\\pi /2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446905} {:answer/id #uuid "41e5d50b-2d0d-5687-83c8-c9e67c35fd0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}({4}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446908} {:answer/id #uuid "bb736353-f883-5d04-8785-134a0e8d1393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}({4}^{\\pi /2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446916} {:answer/id #uuid "fa0493e8-3b12-50f8-9fc2-390aa24a534b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}({4}^{\\pi }-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41e5d50b-2d0d-5687-83c8-c9e67c35fd0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}({4}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446908} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e112384-cbab-5d5f-b556-741daf47c239" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446926}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "53d69396-ad38-5399-a95d-de36a99debd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-103848" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the polar curve $r={4}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={4}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }={4}^{\\theta }\\operatorname{ln}⁡4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{({4}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{({4}^{\\theta }\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{4}^{2\\theta }+{4}^{2\\theta }{ln}^{2}⁡4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(1+{ln}^{2}⁡4){4}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{4}^{\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\cdot {4}^{\\theta }{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\cdot ({4}^{\\pi /2}-{4}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}({4}^{\\pi /2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446933 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0934e304-801c-5c0d-8b01-386d6337214b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta ))^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446903} {:answer/id #uuid "33a0bdd4-e800-5d6d-849a-fb395e74e06a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}({sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )+25{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446906} {:answer/id #uuid "71985b22-a29a-5e8e-a361-5aa92a2495cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )+25{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446909} {:answer/id #uuid "b8da428a-8a49-5ad1-b789-ffb6514c0b70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446915} {:answer/id #uuid "cdce5e1a-03fe-5258-9d66-a128329565d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )+5{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71985b22-a29a-5e8e-a361-5aa92a2495cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )+25{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446909} :answer-field/id #uuid "48332077-b3d7-5599-9447-7b3caa313948" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446927}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7a42296f-57b5-52e8-abcc-dbabb67e9573" :question/math-academy-id "q-15121" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{5}?$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta ),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta ))^{2}+(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )+25{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446934 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ea5acb7-0ee2-5efa-9cb6-56917fa73a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446913} {:answer/id #uuid "91b14c4c-3ed0-52f0-a3ee-ae78598ce9a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446914} {:answer/id #uuid "dde56d65-c679-5147-bb10-2f5b7354e62d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446920} {:answer/id #uuid "f5d38d23-26ec-5c2a-a257-830016a32749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446921} {:answer/id #uuid "fb78dc11-cc0d-583f-b9e3-429b039a2c4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb78dc11-cc0d-583f-b9e3-429b039a2c4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446923} :answer-field/id #uuid "f44e970c-d097-5c6c-a97c-5ef5ce4b1558" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "954fde1b-bd90-5ee0-826c-b4121bc79ca3" :question/math-academy-id "q-9538" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the polar curve $r=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to use the following identity: $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}.\n$$*" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall the identity for $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right):$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using $x=\\theta $ in the previous identity, the integral can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={2(-2)(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right))|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-4(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1) \\\\  & =4-2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446935 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ebaec30-3483-55e2-9524-7055da0607e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ebaec30-3483-55e2-9524-7055da0607e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446907} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b76675c-e686-504c-9fa2-4f4538262ff5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f471af72-8928-5fe0-b630-625d8128766a" :question/math-academy-id "q-347923" :question/problem "![](images/81/81632c931b0846520a056a872cdf327b9031fea4e3b91bf2374973fff1a2354b.png)\n\nFind the arc length $L$ of the polar curve $r=3+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above). Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint: You may wish to use the following identity: $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}.\n$$*\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=3+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{(3+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{9+18\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +9{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +9{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3i}\\sqrt{18+18\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall the identity for $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right):$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using $x=\\theta $ in the previous identity, the integral can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =3\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={6\\cdot 2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right))|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =12(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =12(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499484 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39bd8942-8ea6-5f03-b9c2-980c08387095" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{10}}{3}({e}^{3\\pi /2}+{e}^{-3\\pi /2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498858} {:answer/id #uuid "3f95ea7f-6aac-57fb-89fc-e3618b1effd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\sqrt{10}}{3}{e}^{3\\pi /2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498876} {:answer/id #uuid "472465ce-5697-565a-b045-a23526f9815c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}({e}^{2\\pi /3}-{e}^{-2\\pi /3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498893} {:answer/id #uuid "a7929dc7-bc71-5a90-8bb2-c5a85e81928b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{10}}{3}({e}^{3\\pi /2}-{e}^{-3\\pi /2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499099} {:answer/id #uuid "e97e245e-6898-5e7c-8a99-3baaa90c0589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}{e}^{3\\pi /2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7929dc7-bc71-5a90-8bb2-c5a85e81928b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{10}}{3}({e}^{3\\pi /2}-{e}^{-3\\pi /2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499099} :answer-field/id #uuid "62f08aa4-9c3b-5881-9036-fcd624473552" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "657b78ff-bfd8-5861-b182-c1815c474783" :question/math-academy-id "q-9534" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the polar curve $r=2{e}^{3\\theta }$ for $$\n\\displaystyle -\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2{e}^{3\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=6{e}^{3\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{(2{e}^{3\\theta })}^{2}+{(6{e}^{3\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{4{e}^{6\\theta }+36{e}^{6\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{40{e}^{6\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{10}}{3}{e}^{3\\theta }{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{10}}{3}({e}^{3\\pi /2}-{e}^{-3\\pi /2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499502 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0989efb5-1038-59ac-8680-60117382e68a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{(\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )+1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498746} {:answer/id #uuid "1ce9d6eb-3f8f-56eb-a2d0-a4cfacaf7268" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+2(\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )+2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498792} {:answer/id #uuid "38d06719-2aef-52ec-b523-72bbe2d5ce07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )+1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498855} {:answer/id #uuid "51cc30b4-2098-5551-9641-1f9551e409a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+2(\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )+2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498920} {:answer/id #uuid "52b44f14-c340-50a7-9cae-50d08c357aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+(\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )+1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51cc30b4-2098-5551-9641-1f9551e409a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+2(\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )+2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498920} :answer-field/id #uuid "f107053f-9248-55df-a0bd-cf3499751023" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499425}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "85d77d15-6969-5117-952d-e2b202d58514" :question/math-academy-id "q-15123" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{({\\theta }^{2}+2\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )+(1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+2(\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )+2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499546 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "160e2a0c-f074-5874-a5f2-17cc1fc2cae2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{1-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +5{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498777} {:answer/id #uuid "6d20f288-51ab-5e95-ad79-fa5df49f89a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{3-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498973} {:answer/id #uuid "a35283a7-4adc-5de1-826d-87a387cd4479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499081} {:answer/id #uuid "c87b6998-b8e9-5934-9893-be14c9c09927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{5+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499169} {:answer/id #uuid "d102d768-01d6-510f-bd39-ea2452eac6cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{3+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a35283a7-4adc-5de1-826d-87a387cd4479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499081} :answer-field/id #uuid "cafcbac5-e575-5e1d-93e5-5e527facd2e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d774fdc1-484c-5e5e-b140-afbc35a348d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-51202" :question/problem "![](images/87/87a3563153fe0310767a79a96df0df5f6c0824027776b761df4a792b8b9b235e.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi $ (shown in blue in the diagram above)?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531565 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "138e119b-9f29-5728-b024-f296e1407436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3+{ln}^{2}⁡2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({3}^{\\pi }-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530898} {:answer/id #uuid "4c63f797-f964-543b-8948-8fa3ef071043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}({3}^{\\pi }+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531027} {:answer/id #uuid "6b6ad79e-00af-5e1d-b171-f99e8a87b59c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}}({3}^{\\pi }-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531103} {:answer/id #uuid "a24f9d67-8d4f-5f04-a33c-d625d9ff53b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}({3}^{\\pi }-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531215} {:answer/id #uuid "ee47508c-c5ac-50f6-8486-05ab49b69007" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}({3}^{\\pi }-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee47508c-c5ac-50f6-8486-05ab49b69007" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}({3}^{\\pi }-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531346} :answer-field/id #uuid "770387f5-8ab3-56b6-9ab8-582f315d1f1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1bd5daf3-8ee2-5ee2-ae53-b882ce969a04" :question/math-academy-id "q-9541" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the polar curve $r={3}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={3}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }={3}^{\\theta }\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{({3}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{({3}^{\\theta }\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{3}^{2\\theta }+{3}^{2\\theta }{ln}^{2}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(1+{ln}^{2}⁡3){3}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{3}^{\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot {3}^{\\theta }{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot ({3}^{\\pi }-{3}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}({3}^{\\pi }-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531606 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ebc83588-25b8-5ff4-bfc0-bce39c4a0f4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{10}(e^{\\pi}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebc83588-25b8-5ff4-bfc0-bce39c4a0f4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{10}(e^{\\pi}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531337} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d00646e-dd97-589c-8e21-634590dfdfc6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531395}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6ddfe515-d085-541a-8dab-b3a5ab40f555" :question/math-academy-id "q-353601" :question/problem "![](images/ec/ec0b88ec00ef7e7061af0b08761eb73f05a5f669208babacbd4eb86736019230.png)\n\nFind the arc length $L$ of the polar curve $r=6{e}^{3\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=6{e}^{3\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=18{e}^{3\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{(6{e}^{3\\theta })}^{2}+{(18{e}^{3\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{36{e}^{6\\theta }+324{e}^{6\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{360{e}^{6\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{10}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}{e}^{3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{10}{[\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3\\theta }]}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}{[{e}^{3\\theta }]}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}({e}^{\\pi }-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}({e}^{\\pi }-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531626 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15a09810-6e1e-5a7f-a496-a308672d8fe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530902} {:answer/id #uuid "70d61664-e8b3-5d91-831f-2ef5a133d2af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531115} {:answer/id #uuid "75c79860-2158-5faa-be6a-5b9aa2eb7054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531123} {:answer/id #uuid "931cc387-4c8e-5435-8982-a4705188d119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531181} {:answer/id #uuid "ad39fb78-7dc8-5c7f-b6cd-c9732f59d8ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad39fb78-7dc8-5c7f-b6cd-c9732f59d8ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531238} :answer-field/id #uuid "452ad711-f8a6-5c7b-b980-01feac5bbbde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a1c1460f-c5a2-5e99-b7f7-17db73e707c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-103828" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}?$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{(1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )+{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531628 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "901a723b-e6e5-572f-9b48-3f4f2a4dea43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "901a723b-e6e5-572f-9b48-3f4f2a4dea43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531175} :answer-field/id #uuid "3487b8fc-2024-52a0-8191-9d6c368ac790" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531427}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a9290c4e-ece3-5a58-aecc-bb62b4894116" :question/math-academy-id "q-353582" :question/problem "![](images/83/83813bff1ff86036e2773d9476150de619688daec9cae2623a555a43290cace3.png)\n\nFind the arc length $L$ of the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{5\\pi }{6}\n$$ (shown in blue in the diagram above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +9{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{9}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}3\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531644 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ce61a52-02f8-52e3-833d-f0a747be827a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}({2}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530920} {:answer/id #uuid "25efba17-6780-5d23-af19-6462827fe365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({2}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530950} {:answer/id #uuid "44549959-713e-5a87-987f-4262b4d5d3c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\sqrt{2}}({2}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531009} {:answer/id #uuid "ca7da443-446d-582f-b934-dcaf57f4a7d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({2}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531287} {:answer/id #uuid "d25fbccb-dafe-5557-83e3-f260cee1b53a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}({2}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25efba17-6780-5d23-af19-6462827fe365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({2}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530950} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a4caf7b-52fc-5e88-b891-82cc9a3a2cf7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "da080066-6980-5e46-a310-b96dc7f7120c" :question/math-academy-id "q-9540" :question/problem "![](images/c1/c1bf9d989f1fbaeda90325b924f2c9285cd4e37e1948ba63256258b0a84c7e44.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r={2}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={2}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }={2}^{\\theta }\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{({2}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{({2}^{\\theta }\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{2}^{2\\theta }+{2}^{2\\theta }{ln}^{2}⁡2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(1+{ln}^{2}⁡2){2}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{2}^{\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot {2}^{\\theta }{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot ({2}^{\\pi /2}-{2}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({2}^{\\pi /2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536832 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ada2e3d-0769-5b5a-85e6-218cbeec1c89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536348} {:answer/id #uuid "4b33b710-8754-5317-ad8d-edc5c3f9305d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536402} {:answer/id #uuid "725bc856-b7c0-56dc-9518-bdc1f5428c77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536473} {:answer/id #uuid "cc05201a-8232-5a04-8ce3-e3ac354a9f76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536605} {:answer/id #uuid "f6d4553a-62e1-59c9-8854-5587cc1e9c71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "725bc856-b7c0-56dc-9518-bdc1f5428c77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536473} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6fa46cf-d1f0-5fd4-a76c-c62db6438a9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "50970995-9b99-52ed-ae6b-c20b930d578c" :question/math-academy-id "q-9537" :question/problem "![](images/50/5034bb902aadd151cc1a28764e054dbdd6a694ad653f50557e5fc208c8ec2342.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi $ (shown in blue in the diagram above).\n\n*Hint: You may wish to use the following identity: $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}.\n$$*" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall the identity for $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right):$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}\n$$\n\nUsing $x=\\theta $ in the above identity, the integral can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={2\\cdot 2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right))|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =4(1-0) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19a8a941-abee-5eec-a85d-2c36090c0c9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+2{e}^{\\theta }(\\theta +1)+{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547369} {:answer/id #uuid "829b49d5-b322-53c3-b0f4-1c6304fa46ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}-2{e}^{\\theta }-2{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547594} {:answer/id #uuid "c107c606-2649-543d-89fe-4a7928489ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}-2{e}^{\\theta }(1-\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547735} {:answer/id #uuid "c4d84b89-ed7c-5866-bbe7-886aa45f00d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+2{e}^{\\theta }(\\theta +1)+2{e}^{2\\theta }+1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547741} {:answer/id #uuid "fceb4866-634d-53f1-b923-46c9e70b07f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+2\\theta {e}^{\\theta }+2{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4d84b89-ed7c-5866-bbe7-886aa45f00d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+2{e}^{\\theta }(\\theta +1)+2{e}^{2\\theta }+1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547741} :answer-field/id #uuid "17a97da4-f06a-512c-b0f2-d273f0e4876b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8023cebc-048b-5288-9c32-1da095db126f" :question/math-academy-id "q-103827" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=\\theta +{e}^{\\theta }$ for $-\\pi \\le \\theta \\le \\pi ?$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\theta +{e}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=1+{e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(\\theta +{e}^{\\theta })^{2}+(1+{e}^{\\theta })^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+2\\theta {e}^{\\theta }+{e}^{2\\theta }+1+2{e}^{\\theta }+{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+2{e}^{\\theta }(\\theta +1)+2{e}^{2\\theta }+1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604612 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54d84057-3f42-5b84-9665-912383bc8c65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604308} {:answer/id #uuid "aefd31d4-6f9f-5764-a800-7217b761bebd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604396} {:answer/id #uuid "c2d8a4ec-bf0e-5b71-a3e5-b591def97ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604415} {:answer/id #uuid "dc1e3829-f5d9-5b85-9f4e-3ed45d43c8ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604440} {:answer/id #uuid "dee085d4-3520-538f-bcd4-b1b55e15cc22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc1e3829-f5d9-5b85-9f4e-3ed45d43c8ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604440} :answer-field/id #uuid "047438fe-a241-5674-8589-5b12a12fa274" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "abc9c874-920c-5bcd-917e-8820d313588d" :question/math-academy-id "q-9533" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\theta {|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186637331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e1938ca-1740-5ec7-a527-9a6ae1343572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e1938ca-1740-5ec7-a527-9a6ae1343572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636912} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a7466a6-3996-5fa0-9fe2-c358549417e2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fad42fe8-b9b3-5e70-b2aa-4790ce691d7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-167954" :question/problem "Construct and simplify an integral representing the arc length of this circle using polar coordinates.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }$\n{{field-1}} $\\,\\,\\text{d}\\theta$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=12\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta$, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=12\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(12\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(12\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(12\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{12}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }12\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
